{{!--
  Sent to an account's address when a session of it was signed out after
  too many wrong attempts to confirm it was its owner's (#10218, Confirm
  It's You, Common/Server/Utils/Reauthentication/SignedOutEmail): a wrong
  password, code, backup code, security key or passkey, from a session
  that was already signed in - the clearest sign there is that somebody
  else holds it. One email per session signed out, and a few a day at most.

  It says what happened and when, in the reader's time zone; from where
  the attempt that ended the session came (the rows of
  Partials/RequestOriginFields.hbs, which show only what is known); that
  the account is not locked; and what to do if it was not them: a new
  password, which signs every device out (hasPassword), or their
  organization's admin, for an account that signs in with single sign-on.

  The product's name goes into a sentence through ttHtml, which escapes the
  whole sentence; the time is a value. Everything else is OneUptime's own
  words, looked up in the reader's language (Utils/EmailLanguage.ts).
--}}

{{> EmailTitle title=(t "A session of your account was signed out") }}

{{> InfoBlock info=(ttHtml "A session signed in to your {{product}} account was asked to confirm it was you, and got it wrong too many times, so it has been signed out." product=(brandName))}}

{{> InfoBlock info=(tHtml "Your account is not locked: you can sign in as usual.")}}

{{> DetailBoxStart this }}
{{> DetailBoxField title=(t "Signed out at:") plainText=signedOutAt }}
{{> RequestOriginFields this }}
{{> DetailBoxEnd this }}

{{> InfoBlock info=(tHtml "If this was you, sign in again to carry on.")}}

{{#if hasPassword}}
{{> InfoBlock info=(tHtml "If this was not you, someone else had that session and may still be able to sign in to your account. Reset your password: a new password signs every device out of your account.")}}

{{> ButtonBlock buttonText=(t "Reset your password") buttonUrl=forgotPasswordUrl }}
{{else}}
{{> InfoBlock info=(tHtml "If this was not you, someone else had that session and may still be able to sign in to your account. Tell your organization's admin right away.")}}
{{/if}}

{{> SupportBlock this}}

{{> Footer this}}

{{> End this}}
